{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q83034468","formula":"C₂₀H₂₁N₃O","hill":"C20H21N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":21.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"LEK 8842"},"descriptions":{"en":"LEK-8842, also known as N-methyl-N-(2-propynyl)lysergamide or as TRALA-01, is a serotonin receptor modulator of the lysergamide family related to the psychedelic drug LSD. The drug is described as showing serotonin 5-HT2 receptor partial agonistic activity and α-adrenergic receptor agonistic activity based on in-vitro tissue assays that included selective antagonist challenges. Subsequently, it was found to be a potent partial agonist of the serotonin 5-HT2A and 5-HT2B receptors and to show affinity for the serotonin 5-HT2C receptor. LEK-8842 produces effects in animals including serotonin behavioral syndrome, hyperthermia, pressor effects, pupil dilation, and uterine contractions."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":164461,"mass":319.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1C[C@@H](C=C2[C@H]1CC3=CNC4=CC=CC2=C34)C(=O)N(C)CC#C","inchikey":"NTIBYWGZNANJNM-RDTXWAMCSA-N","iupac":"(6aR,9R)-N,7-dimethyl-N-prop-2-ynyl-6,6a,8,9-tetrahydro-4H-indolo[4,3-fg]quinoline-9-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"164461","atoms":45,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.827,"y":0.502,"z":-1.295,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.116,"y":-2.459,"z":-0.034,"el":"N"},{"x":5.269,"y":0.185,"z":0.068,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.968,"y":0.286,"z":0.718,"el":"N"},{"x":0.988,"y":-1.518,"z":-0.375,"el":"C"},{"x":0.682,"y":-0.046,"z":0.034,"el":"C"},{"x":2.337,"y":-2.058,"z":0.229,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.698,"y":-0.629,"z":0.442,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.423,"y":-1.887,"z":-0.386,"el":"C"},{"x":3.409,"y":-1.03,"z":0.144,"el":"C"},{"x":1.798,"y":0.925,"z":-0.013,"el":"C"},{"x":3.065,"y":0.334,"z":0.039,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.545,"y":0.327,"z"